														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851461">
									

<p>Hello everyone! I'm Ross - although you can call me Mira too, if you'd like!</p>
<p>I'm 20 years old, and I've been been a casual reader of SCP articles for what must be almost five or six years now. Recently, though, I've delved far deeper into the assorted canons and some of the less &quot;popular&quot; articles, and I'm amazed by just how much the site really has to offer.</p>
<p>I enjoy the tone of the SCP Wiki on the whole - the general style is one that I am not particularly good at writing, but enjoy reading to a great extent. The creativity on display in exploring concepts from the harmlessly light-hearted to the ones so horrifying that they have stuck with me for years is nothing short of admirable. (Perhaps one day, I'll workshop an idea of my own, but that isn't likely to happen for a very long time.)</p>
<p>As far as hobbies go, I enjoy character design and writing, and as some have likely deduced from my username, I'm a huge fan of visual novels as well. I also like baking, although most baked goods tend to be a little too sweet for my personal tastes.</p>
<p>With regards to what kind of random thoughts keep me up at night, they tend to range from something as mundane as having a song stuck in my head to whatever catastrophic situations my tired, anxious mind is able to come up with. Typically, though, they'll just jump from one topic of interest to another - usually if I've read something I really enjoyed, I won't be able to stop thinking about it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
