<p>So uh&#8230; This may or may not be useful, but as I'm sure you know, in the nineteenth century there were all kinds of crazy &quot;cures&quot; for mental illness. One that really stands out as particularly crazy was called the Cox's Chair. It was basically a chair you would strap someone in, then spin the chair around really, really fast. (Like spinning in an office chair, except more intense.) You would then stop the chair suddenly, in the hope that the illness would be forcefully jerked out of the patient. (It didn't work) So if what you were looking for was an entity that tries to help people, but sort of&#8230; screws up, Cox's Chair could be an interesting edition. I hope you find what you're looking for, and good luck on your scip!</p>

							</div>

								
					
