<p>1) A minor problem is that this makes another reset option and that it has been used twice before. If it hadn't been tied in to &quot;narrative&quot;, it wouldn't have been noticed.</p>
<p>2) As a science geek, there's my usual issue involving singularities: Their very presence planetside should be causing a lot of problems, especially one that's going to go Big Bang. If it's just going to increase its density, then that means that it's going to be a problem well before it explodes. That is was found with just a stone tablet just makes it even sillier (if it sucks in nearby matter/energy at a subatomic level, why would the stone tablet last that long?).</p>
<p>3) Given the sheer number of alien races and dimensional links that the SCP deals with, this is not as big a problem as it may seem: Just have an alien race looking for a power source pick it up or dimensionally displace it to a dead universe. If the alien that put it down comes around looking for it, just give him the coordinates.</p>
<p>It's a neat idea, but it's going to be neutralized quickly. It has to be.</p>

